observations.description:
4.1 We looked into the JVA of the CGM with JBROS Construction Corporation (JBROS for brevity) for the Arroceros Compound Mixed-Use Development Project to: (a) establish adherence to the Manila JVO No. 8346; and (b) performance by the parties of their respective obligations under this JVA.

4.2 Section 15 of the Manila JVO, maps out a three-stage framework, to which negotiated JV Agreements are to be mandatorily subjected, viz:

Stage One/Unsolicited Proposal xxx

xxx

Stage Two/Detailed Negotiations xxx

xxx

Stage Three/Swiss Challenge xxx

xxx

4.3 A Swiss Challenge is "a hybrid mechanism between the direct negotiation approach and the competitive bidding route. The Swiss Challenge is a system where "[a] third party can bid on a project during a designated period but the original proponent can counter match any superior offer. It is a form of public bidding.

4.4 In our letter to the Management dated 04 December 2020, we requested documents pertinent to the JVA between the CGM and JBROS for the Arroceros Compound Mixed-Used Development Project. The Records Division, City General Services Office (central repository of the official documents of the CGM) in its reply dated 10 December 2020, submitted a Certification that a photocopy of the JVA, consisting of 15 pages, is the only document existing in their Office file and without the supporting Annexes.

4.5 In a letter dated 16 December 2020, the City Legal Officer submitted certified true copies of the following documents relative to the JVA with JBROS:

a. Executive Order No. 25, series of 2016, An Order Reconstituting the Joint Venture Selection Committee (JV-SC) pursuant to City Ordinance No. 8346;

b. JBROS Letter dated 10 March 2017 to then City Mayor Joseph Ejercito Estrada regarding the Unsolicited Proposal for the Arroceros Compound Mixed-Use Development Project;

c. Letter dated 13 March 2017 to JBROS from Atty. Edward S. Serapio, then Secretary to the Mayor and Chairman of JV-SC acknowledging the Unsolicited Proposal;

d. JV-SC Resolution dated 14 March 2017 determining the completeness of the Unsolicited Proposal, approved by then City Mayor Estrada;

e. JV-SC Letter dated 15 March 2017 to JBROS regarding Declaration of Completeness of the Unsolicited Proposal;

f. JV-SC Letter dated 16 March 2017 to the City Council of Manila requesting for authority to enter into negotiations through JV-SC;

g. JV-SC Notice of Meeting dated 21 March 2017 for the evaluation of the Unsolicited Proposal;

h. City Council Resolution No, 72, series of 2017 adopted on 30 March 2017 authorizing then City Mayor Estrada to enter into a negotiation most advantageous to the City through JVA;

i. JV-SC Resolution dated 23 March 2017 on evaluating the Unsolicited Proposal and recommending to then City Mayor Estrada to accept the same and to declare JBROS as the original proponent for the Arroceros Compound development project;

j. JV-SC Letter dated 24 March 2017, Declaration as Original Proponent for the same development project;

k. Joint Certification dated 18 April 2017 of then City Mayor Estrada for the City of Manila and JBROS President, Engr Jesusito B. Legaspi, Jr., attested by the Chairman JV-SC;

l. JV-SC Resolution dated 18 April 2017, inclusion of revisions on the Draft JVA and approved by then City Mayor Estrada;

m. JV-SC Letter dated 18 April 2017 to JBROS on Posting of Proposal Security;

n. JV-SC Invitation to Submit Comparative Proposals, Apply for Eligibility and if Eligible To Bid/Submit Proposals for the Arroceros Compound Mixed-Use Development Project;

o. JBROS Performance Bond No. G(13)-A000415 issued by Western Guaranty Corporation amounting to P75Million, notarized on 24 April 2017;

p. Certification dated 25 April 2017 by Atty. Serapio, then Secretary to the City Mayor on Posting of the Invitation to Submit Comparative Proposal for the Arroceros project on the Bulletin Boards of the Offices of the Secretary to the Mayor and CGSO for the duration 25 April 2017 to 02 May 2017;

q. Affidavit of Publication on 25 April 2017 and 02 May 2017 of the Invitation to Submit Comparative Proposals etc., by the Advertising Coordinator of The Daily Tribune.;

r. JV-SC dated 26 May 2017 recommending the Award of the development project to JBROS, approved by then City Mayor Estrada;

s. Notice of Award dated 29 May 2017, JBROS Conforme dated 30 May 2017 and signed by JBROS President Legaspi;

t. JV-SC Notice of Award signed by Atty. Serapio and approved by then City Mayor Estrada, Dates of Publication: 31 May 2017 and 07 June 2017;

u. Atty. Serapio’s Letter dated 31 May 2017, noted by then City Mayor Estrada to the City Council of Manila on the Request for Public Hearing and Ratification;

v. City Council Resolution No. 152, series of 2017 ratifying the JVA adopted on 06 June 2017;

w. JBROS Western Guaranty Corporation (WGC) Performance Bond No. G(13)-022520 for P75 Million notarized on 01 June 2017;

x. WGC Certification on the validity and authenticity of the Performance Bond No. G(13)-022520;

y. Bank Guaranty dated 01 June 2017 issued by East West bank for P7.725Billion;

z. Affidavit of Publication of the Notice of Award on 31 May 2017 and 07 June 2017 by the Advertising Coordinator of The Daily Tribune;

aa. JBROS Undertaking notarized on 01 June 2017, Makati City; and

ab. JVA, signed and notarized on 16 June 2017.

4.6 Stage Three/Swiss Challenge procedure as articulated in the Manila JVO, requires the preparation of the following documents:

a. Tender documents which include among others, Instruction to Bidders, Terms of Reference, draft JVA, Bid Form, Forms of Bid and Performance Securities, requirements and timelines, other documents as may be deemed necessary by the JV-SC;

b. Publication of the Invitation for Comparative Proposals in at least one newspaper of general circulation;

c. Posting of the Invitation for Comparative Proposals in two conspicuous places in the City;

d. Posting of the Invitation for Comparative Proposals in the City's Official Website, if available;

e. Posting of the Proposal Security by the Original Proponent; and

f. Proposals Submitted by the challengers.

4.7 Review of the JVA documents vis-à-vis those required in the Manila JVO showed that the following were not submitted to the Audit Team:

a. Tender documents;

b. Copy of The Daily Tribune newspapers or page/s thereof where the notices/invites were published;

c. Time-stamped pictures of the postings; and

d. Time-stamped screenshot of the postings.

4.8 As to the documents in b and c of para. 4.7, the CGM submitted only a Certification of the previous JV-SC Chairperson of the postings of the Invitation to Submit Comparative Proposal for the Arroceros project on the Bulletin Boards of the Offices of the Secretary to the Mayor and CGSO, and an affidavit executed by the Advertising Coordinator of the of The Daily Tribune newspaper that the Invitation to Submit Comparative Proposal for the Arroceros project was published on 25 April 2017 and 2 May 2017. These certification and affidavit, however, are different from the required documents themselves because it is a documents merely authenticating the latter. The publication and the posting of the Invitation for Comparative Proposals are very vital in the conduct of the Stage Three/Swiss Challenge since it is the best means of securing a comparative proposal which is superior or more advantageous than the original proposal and to ensure that the government gets the best benefit/return.

4.9 Upon our inquiry, The Tribune Publishing Co. Inc (The Tribune for brevity) informed that they have no record of the subject publications because this record was not endorsed by the previous management and that their record is only from June 2018. We were also informed that the person supposedly responsible for the attendant publications, is no longer connected with The Tribune.

4.10 Verily, the unsubmitted documents listed in para. 4.7 supporting the JVA with JBROS for the Arroceros Compound Mixed-Use Development prevented the full evaluation of and casts doubt on the validity of the Swiss Challenge to which such joint venture project was subjected.

The continuing failure of the JBROS to perform its obligations under the JVA deprives the CGM beneficial use of the Arroceros Compound.

4.11 Under Section 10.1 of the Arroceros Compound JVA, either party may rescind the JVA prior to its completion upon default or breach by the other party of a material provision of the JVA.

4.12 On 16 June 2017, the CGM entered into agreement with JBROS to redevelop the Arroceros into a mixed residential-mall-office complex with enhanced recreational area with an estimated total project cost of P5,646,491,950.000. The term of the construction and development is estimated to be within seven (7) years divided into four (4) phases. The phase one (1) which consists of the construction of the mall and a government center building is estimated to be completed on year 3. Moreover, phase two (2) which consists of the Office Building shall be undertaken by JBROS on year 3.

4.13 However, in his letter dated 09 March 2021, the City Engineer informed us that the said project has not started. Almost four years had passed from the date of the effectivity of the JVA but JBROS failed to deliver Phases one and two of the project. Over this period, the CGM has been deprived of the beneficial use of its investment in this joint venture, namely: Arroceros Compound, with gross lot area of 10,134.40 square meters.

4.14 This material breach is a ground for rescission pursuant to Section 10.1 of the JVA, subject to the provisions of Section 12 on Dispute Resolution.

The CGM has not fully protected its interest by its failure to require JBROS to post performance bond covering the period within which the latter is obligated to complete the joint venture project.

4.15 Section 18 of the Manila JVO requires the posting of performance security 20 days from official receipt of the "Notice of Award", which we believe, a conferment of the authority to the City Mayor and the JV-SC in the determination of the appropriate performance security in relation to Section 14.h.ii.(6) of the same Ordinance on bid security where the City was given the authority to determine what form of bid security it will require.

4.16 JBROS posted a Performance Bond under Western Guaranty Corporation No. G(13)022520 in the amount of P75 million to guarantee the faithful performance of the obligations for the Arroceros Compound Mixed Use Development Project and in compliance with Section 18 of the City of Manila Ordinance No. 8346, a condition stated in the Notice of Award where the consortium is required to file a performance security (Bond) prior to the signing and ratification of the JVA. The bond is callable on demand and valid from date of issuance until six month automatically renewable for another six months. The liability of the Surety under the Bond shall in no case exceed the total sum of P75 million. It was notarized on 01 June 2017. The bond expired on 01 December 2017.

4.17 It is our view that the CGM failed to protect reasonably its interest in the JVA by not requiring JBROS to extend the validity of the foregoing bond to, at the very least, cover the period over which JBROS is obligated to complete Phases One and Two of the development project.

4.18 While the CGM transferred control of the Arroceros Compound (with gross lot area of 10,134.40 square meters) to the joint venture in faithful performance of its obligation under the JVA, JBROS failed to deliver the Phases One and Two of the development project for almost four years already, to date. Over these four-years, the CGM suffered opportunity loss as it had no beneficial use of the Arroceros Compound. Had the JVA been bonded adequately, this opportunity loss could have been avoided.
